DAT
id=qid::label=str::text=lstr::
22925::$$$message_0178_0000_0000$$$::I wonder how many resurrections this makes.[lr]::
22926::$$$message_0178_0000_0001$$$::I hear voices.[lr]::
22927::$$$message_0178_0000_0002$$$::It's a grudge directed at me. Me, drowning in death repeatedly only to be spit back out.[lr]::
22928::$$$message_0178_0000_0003$$$::They can't escape death, so they call it unfair that I can.::
22929::$$$message_0178_0001_0000$$$::My whole body hurts. It hurts so bad I can't breathe. The voices attack and blame me. [wait canskip=false time=1000]DIE. [wait canskip=false time=600]GIVE UP. [wait canskip=false time=600]SERVES YOU RIGHT. [wait canskip=false time=600]CAN'T SEE. [wait canskip=false time=600]They become stronger each time I hear them. [wait canskip=false time=1500]I want to die. [wait canskip=false time=600]I can't take this. [wait canskip=false time=600]HIDEOUS. [wait canskip=false time=600]DISGUSTING. [wait canskip=false time=600]CAN'T SEE ANYMORE. [wait canskip=false time=600]i wAnT TO DiE. [wait canskip=false time=600]I don't want to hear this. [wait canskip=false time=1000]I don't want to come back to life, if this is how heavy it feels.::
22930::$$$message_0178_0002_0000$$$::But I'm used to even that, now.::
22931::$$$message_0178_0003_0000$$$::DIE.[nolr][br][rf][wait canskip=0 time=500]::
22932::$$$message_0178_0003_0001$$$::                                       Hurry up and kill me.[lr]::
22933::$$$message_0178_0003_0002$$$::THAt'S THE sPiRIT.[nolr][br][rf][wait canskip=0 time=500]::
22934::$$$message_0178_0003_0003$$$::                                       Just enjoy what you like.[lr]::
22935::$$$message_0178_0003_0004$$$::rEpeNt.[nolr][br][rf][wait canskip=0 time=500]::
22936::$$$message_0178_0003_0005$$$::                                       Yes, I've already done that a number of times.[lr]::
22937::$$$message_0178_0003_0006$$$::IT'S YOUR FAULT.[nolr][br][rf][wait canskip=0 time=500]::
22938::$$$message_0178_0003_0007$$$::                                       Yes, it's all someone's fault.[lr]::
22939::$$$message_0178_0003_0008$$$::HOW FiLThY.[nolr][br][rf][wait canskip=0 time=500]::
22940::$$$message_0178_0003_0009$$$::                                       I'm not trying to put on a show.::
22941::$$$message_0178_0004_0000$$$::yOU're NOT HuMAn.[nolr][br][rf][wait canskip=0 time=500]::
22942::$$$message_0178_0004_0001$$$::                                       ...This mirror is foggy.[lr]::
22943::$$$message_0178_0004_0002$$$::yOu DEmon.[nolr][br][rf][wait canskip=0 time=500]::
22944::$$$message_0178_0004_0003$$$::                                  Yeah... I'm not behaving like a human.::
22945::$$$message_0178_0005_0000$$$::I pass a multitude of voices and begin to breathe again.[lr]::
22946::$$$message_0178_0005_0001$$$::...The next part isn't too painful. It's comforting, even. As long as I escape from that prison, the rest of my resurrection is almost joyous.::
22947::$$$message_0178_0006_0000$$$::Prison. Yes, that would be an accurate term for it.[lr]::
22948::$$$message_0178_0006_0001$$$::Slander. Abuse. Contempt.[lr]::
22949::$$$message_0178_0006_0002$$$::Rights robbed. Dignity deprived. Liberty lost.[lr]::
22950::$$$message_0178_0006_0003$$$::Surely basically everybody has heard that the afterlife is made up of such ideas.[lr]::
22951::$$$message_0178_0006_0004$$$::Perpetual suffering.[lr]::
22952::$$$message_0178_0006_0005$$$::Buddhism calls it the Avici hell.::
22953::$$$message_0178_0007_0000$$$::...But the place I occupied was subtly different.[lr]::
22954::$$$message_0178_0007_0001$$$::It wasn't only suffering;[lr]::
22955::$$$message_0178_0007_0002$$$::it was eternally empty.[lr]::
22956::$$$message_0178_0007_0003$$$::Human hands can't reach either place, nor is there any point to doing so.[lr]::
22957::$$$message_0178_0007_0004$$$::That's why it's suffering.[lr]::
22958::$$$message_0178_0007_0005$$$::When humans wish for and obtain something they can't handle, they'll never be able to get rid of it...::
22959::$$$message_0178_0008_0000$$$::"...Ngh..."[lr]::
22960::$$$message_0178_0008_0001$$$::I rise from the sofa.[lr]::
22961::$$$message_0178_0008_0002$$$::Fighting down the despondency of resurrection that I've experienced several times now, I make sure my left arm still works.::
22962::$$$message_0178_0009_0000$$$::"Hey. You're awake, Master."::
22963::$$$message_0178_0010_0000$$$::...My Servant gives me his canned greeting.[lr]::
22964::$$$message_0178_0010_0001$$$::He's seated facing away from me. It looks like he's playing with a puzzle again. It's easy enough to be solved in a matter of minutes, but he seems to have taken a liking to it.[lr]::
22965::$$$message_0178_0010_0002$$$::...That side of him is childish, I think.[lr]::
22966::$$$message_0178_0010_0003$$$::If only his usual behavior reflected such innocence.::
22967::$$$message_0178_0011_0000$$$::"...Just checking, but did I manage a mutual kill on Assassin?"[lr]::
22968::$$$message_0178_0011_0001$$$::"No, he kicked your ass.[lr]::
22969::$$$message_0178_0011_0002$$$::You whiffed your right straight, and then that 'Fantastical Digibrain' Zabaniya blew your head off.[lr]::
22970::$$$message_0178_0011_0003$$$::You should've seen it! As your brain popped, the rest of your upper body went flying.[lr]::
22971::$$$message_0178_0011_0004$$$::What a creative form of murder, turning brains into gunpowder to blow up the body. Why not just rip the brain out instead?"::
22972::$$$message_0178_0012_0000$$$::My Servant is in high spirits.[lr]::
22973::$$$message_0178_0012_0001$$$::"...Ugh."[lr]::
22974::$$$message_0178_0012_0002$$$::I feel sick, imagining myself without my upper body.::
22975::$$$message_0178_0013_0000$$$::...I remember the fight against Assassin.[lr]::
22976::$$$message_0178_0013_0001$$$::I encountered Assassin's Master in the woods behind the school.[lr]::
22977::$$$message_0178_0013_0002$$$::The Master was the only enemy in sight, and we engaged them.::
22978::$$$message_0178_0014_0000$$$::The enemy Master was an expert puppet-user commanding several automata. The lethally-designed French dolls were troublesome, but I'm very familiar with how such puppets are made.[lr]::
22979::$$$message_0178_0014_0001$$$::I was already used to the chaotic battles with the monsters around town, and it was easy to close in on the puppeteer.[lr]::
22980::$$$message_0178_0014_0002$$$::   Unfortunately, one of the puppets was wearing a skull mask.::
22981::$$$message_0178_0015_0000$$$::"Don't tell me it's a Servant!?"[lr]::
22982::$$$message_0178_0015_0001$$$::By the time I noticed, several poisoned needles had already struck me.[lr]::
22983::$$$message_0178_0015_0002$$$::Assassin. This class chooses from a select pool of Heroic Spirits, whose abilities change with each Holy Grail War.[lr]::
22984::$$$message_0178_0015_0003$$$::Apparently, they belonged to the organization from which the very word "assassin" takes its name, hence the myriad collection of trained killers.[lr]::
22985::$$$message_0178_0015_0004$$$::Assassin is a group, not an individual. This time, a short person no taller than an adult's hip was chosen.::
22986::$$$message_0178_0016_0000$$$::...Perhaps that was its actual height in life, or perhaps some aspect of it was emphasized as a Servant.[lr]::
22987::$$$message_0178_0016_0001$$$::Assassin's stature wasn't that of a dwarf from children's bedtime stories, but the lithe form of a gymnast.[lr]::
22988::$$$message_0178_0016_0002$$$::It was like watching a circus clown.[lr]::
22989::$$$message_0178_0016_0003$$$::While it may have been diminutive for a Heroic Spirit, that trait suited its class well.::
22990::$$$message_0178_0017_0000$$$::It was a difficult target, not only because of Presence Concealment, but because there was so little to hit.[lr]::
22991::$$$message_0178_0017_0001$$$::It had to have been one of the quickest Servants, darting in and out of the trees too quickly for the eye to follow.[lr]::
22992::$$$message_0178_0017_0002$$$::On top of that[line len=2]no, this is probably what makes it an [font italic=true]Assassin[font italic=false] at all[line len=2]the enemy had a Noble Phantasm that ensures its target's death.::
22993::$$$message_0178_0018_0000$$$::"Kh...!"[lr]::
22994::$$$message_0178_0018_0001$$$::By the time I realized the terrain disadvantage, the poison had already paralyzed my legs.[lr]::
22995::$$$message_0178_0018_0002$$$::I would've been more confident on an open field with no cover, but I didn't have a good way to deal with all the trees.[lr]::
22996::$$$message_0178_0018_0003$$$::Still, I bet my life on one last gamble.[lr]::
22997::$$$message_0178_0018_0004$$$::I used my left torso as bait to draw Assassin out of the woods.[lr]::
22998::$$$message_0178_0018_0005$$$::Judging that I had no way to counterattack, Assassin bolted toward me from the left.[lr]::
22999::$$$message_0178_0018_0006$$$::I intercepted with every ounce of my will, throwing a desperate right straight.::
23000::$$$message_0178_0019_0000$$$::My timing was flawless.[lr]::
23001::$$$message_0178_0019_0001$$$::Moving with that momentum, Assassin had no way to dodge, and even if it blocked my blow, it wouldn't be able to cancel it out. That was the flaw of its small stature.[lr]::
23002::$$$message_0178_0019_0002$$$::But it easily leapt over my counter-strike anyway.[lr]::
23003::$$$message_0178_0019_0003$$$::Just as my 80 kilometer-per-hour right straight[line len=2]and a counter-punch, on top of that![line len=2]was about to impact the enemy, there was a comical "boop" sound, and it jumped onto my arm.::
23004::$$$message_0178_0020_0000$$$::"...Bollocks."[fadese time=4500 volume=70 storage=se599][lr]::
23005::$$$message_0178_0020_0001$$$::I'm a seasoned fighter, if I say so myself, but I've never seen anyone jump on my arm and start walking toward me.[lr]::
23006::$$$message_0178_0020_0002$$$::It reminded me of those dubious tales of duelists jumping onto an opponent's spear.[lr]::
23007::$$$message_0178_0020_0003$$$::Then, Assassin reached for my face with its left hand...and I blacked out.::
23008::$$$message_0178_0021_0000$$$::"...What a nightmare,"[lr]::
23009::$$$message_0178_0021_0001$$$::I mutter.::
23010::$$$message_0178_0022_0000$$$::"What's up? Still feeling stiff?"[lr]::
23011::$$$message_0178_0022_0001$$$::"No, I feel fine. I'm used to the resurrection by now.[lr]::
23012::$$$message_0178_0022_0002$$$::You're the only thing making me uncomfortable. I just remembered Assassin's hand touching my cheek."[lr]::
23013::$$$message_0178_0022_0003$$$::"Ah. I see, my bad. Not very sensitive of me."::
23014::$$$message_0178_0023_0000$$$::He laughs to himself, still working on the puzzle.[lr]::
23015::$$$message_0178_0023_0001$$$::Are my failures truly that amusing?[lr]::
23016::$$$message_0178_0023_0002$$$::It isn't just teasing.[lr]::
23017::$$$message_0178_0023_0003$$$::He's got a twisted personality, laughing at the strangest and saddest things, no matter who he's talking to.::
23018::$$$message_0178_0024_0000$$$::"...It's fine. I'm used to you, too.[lr]::
23019::$$$message_0178_0024_0001$$$::So, Avenger. Did you bring me back here?"[lr]::
23020::$$$message_0178_0024_0002$$$::"Nope, they got me too. We both got sent back a day, since we both got killed exactly at midnight."[lr]::
23021::$$$message_0178_0024_0003$$$::"..."[lr]::
23022::$$$message_0178_0024_0004$$$::We're not making any progress.[lr]::
23023::$$$message_0178_0024_0005$$$::How many days have passed since I first woke up in this house?[lr]::
23024::$$$message_0178_0024_0006$$$::We still haven't overcome the fourth night.::
23025::$$$message_0178_0025_0000$$$::...I unconsciously clutch the earring in my pocket, feeling my own inadequacy.[lr]::
23026::$$$message_0178_0025_0001$$$::It's like a lucky charm I brought from home. I don't remember why I took it with me, but it must be some protective amulet, if it was tucked away with such care.::
23027::$$$message_0178_0026_0000$$$::"That wasn't your fault, though.[lr]::
23028::$$$message_0178_0026_0001$$$::That Assassin was just too weird. I'm sure I saw your fist connect.[lr]::
23029::$$$message_0178_0026_0002$$$::Still, don't beat yourself up over it.[lr]::
23030::$$$message_0178_0026_0003$$$::You've got me as a handicap. Gotta hand it to you, you still managed to make the enemy use their Noble Phantasm in the first battle."::
23031::$$$message_0178_0027_0000$$$::"That's the excuse of a loser. No matter how well the fight went, we died and didn't gain any..."[lr]::
23032::$$$message_0178_0027_0001$$$::Wait, we did gain something.[lr]::
23033::$$$message_0178_0027_0002$$$::I still haven't taken full advantage of the fact that this Servant can raise the dead.[lr]::
23034::$$$message_0178_0027_0003$$$::As long as I have a pact with him, I can come back to life as many times as necessary.::
23035::$$$message_0178_0028_0000$$$::"I see, this method could work... In fact, you're a weapon. I should use everything in my disposal. We can consider it a draw, then."[lr]::
23036::$$$message_0178_0028_0001$$$::I'll use him to gain intelligence on our enemies, then go into battle fully prepared and win.[lr]::
23037::$$$message_0178_0028_0002$$$::"...We have the advantage, then.[lr]::
23038::$$$message_0178_0028_0003$$$::Now that we know Assassin's unique power, all we need to do is lure them out onto an open field."::
23039::$$$message_0178_0029_0000$$$::I clench my right fist.[lr]::
23040::$$$message_0178_0029_0001$$$::If we keep this up, we won't need to wait for the enemy Masters to lose their fighting strength.[lr]::
23041::$$$message_0178_0029_0002$$$::Victory is all but assured.[lr]::
23042::$$$message_0178_0029_0003$$$::If I defeat each of them fair and square, then even the Association that sent me will at least[line len=2]::
23043::$$$message_0178_0030_0000$$$::"Huh. You're taking this well.[lr]::
23044::$$$message_0178_0030_0001$$$::I thought you'd be down in the dumps that you keep losing or frustrated at how useless I am."[lr]::
23045::$$$message_0178_0030_0002$$$::"Huh...? W-well, you're right, but..."[lr]::
23046::$$$message_0178_0030_0003$$$::...He's right.[lr]::
23047::$$$message_0178_0030_0004$$$::What am I thinking? Just because he can bring me back to life, it doesn't change the fact that I keep losing.::
23048::$$$message_0178_0031_0000$$$::...Things aren't going well.[lr]::
23049::$$$message_0178_0031_0001$$$::Even Assassin could have killed me anytime it wanted.[lr]::
23050::$$$message_0178_0031_0002$$$::Taking my time to investigate the opponents' strengths is just prolonging our showdown.[lr]::
23051::$$$message_0178_0031_0003$$$::It's almost as if... No, it can't be.[lr]::
23052::$$$message_0178_0031_0004$$$::As a mage representing the Association, I can't lose this war.::
23053::$$$message_0178_0032_0000$$$::"Well, it's not as if the days are exactly moving. We're burning all the time we need."[lr]::
23054::$$$message_0178_0032_0001$$$::The Servant stands.[lr]::
23055::$$$message_0178_0032_0002$$$::He heads for the exit, puzzle unfinished.::
23056::$$$message_0178_0033_0000$$$::"Let's keep going, Master. There's still places you haven't looked, right?"[lr]::
23057::$$$message_0178_0033_0001$$$::I stand up from the sofa at his urging.[lr]::
23058::$$$message_0178_0033_0002$$$::I shoulder my pack, grasp the earring in my pocket one more time, and set out to fight the umpteenth day of the Holy Grail War.::
23059::$$$message_0178_0034_0000$$$::As an aside...[lr]::
23060::$$$message_0178_0034_0001$$$::Bazett Fraga McRemitz is a strange woman.::
23061::$$$message_0178_0035_0000$$$::First of all, her exterior and what's within are strange. They don't align.[lr]::
23062::$$$message_0178_0035_0001$$$::Her appearance is to my taste: a mature, cool woman without any weakness.[lr]::
23063::$$$message_0178_0035_0002$$$::But on the inside, she's an insecure coward who trained her body and mind in order to disguise that.[lr]::
23064::$$$message_0178_0035_0003$$$::My speculation[line len=2]no, my personal wish is that she enjoys tormenting herself. No doubt about it. Yeah, that would explain why she's gone to such extraordinary lengths to strengthen herself.[wm canskip=0][wm canskip=0]::
23065::$$$message_0178_0036_0000$$$::She's built up a stubborn armor of seeming "capable," so her external appeal and toughness are the real deal.[lr]::
23066::$$$message_0178_0036_0001$$$::But tragically, a suit of armor needs gaps to be able to move, and sometimes you can glimpse the real Bazett through them.[lr]::
23067::$$$message_0178_0036_0002$$$::I don't need to explain what that looks like. Her insides are as tender as a soft-boiled egg after being protected for such a long time. She's so innocent and naïve I want to take a bite out of her.[wm canskip=0]::
23068::$$$message_0178_0037_0000$$$::Still, though...[lr]::
23069::$$$message_0178_0037_0001$$$::No matter how adorable her insides are, she's spent so many years forging her armor that it's just too strong.[lr]::
23070::$$$message_0178_0037_0002$$$::Once she's on a mission, in battle mode, I'm sure she'd sweep away any male fantasies or desires.[lr]::
23071::$$$message_0178_0037_0003$$$::Take this earlier episode, for example.[wt canskip=0][current withback=false]::
23072::$$$message_0178_0038_0000$$$::"I'm hungry. Let's have a meal."[lr]::
23073::$$$message_0178_0038_0001$$$::It was sudden.[lr]::
23074::$$$message_0178_0038_0002$$$::After butchering three monsters with her fists, Bazett mentioned food as clinically as you might measure someone's pulse.::
23075::$$$message_0178_0039_0000$$$::"You should join me. You must find my magical energy supply dull on its own."[lr]::
23076::$$$message_0178_0039_0001$$$::What a thoughtful Master...[lr]::
23077::$$$message_0178_0039_0002$$$::...or so I thought, until we stepped into the beef bowl restaurant.::
23078::$$$message_0178_0040_0000$$$::"Ugh."[lr]::
23079::$$$message_0178_0040_0001$$$::Even I know this place. It's the restaurant with the biggest and cheapest portions in Shinto.[lr]::
23080::$$$message_0178_0040_0002$$$::Just so you know, there are still plenty of other restaurants open, even though there's less people in Fuyuki now. A more upscale place that would cater to Bazett's tastes is still open just a hundred meters away.[lr]::
23081::$$$message_0178_0040_0003$$$::And yet she chose this place.[lr]::
23082::$$$message_0178_0040_0004$$$::There's no doubt about it; she chose this place because it happened to be the closest.::
23083::$$$message_0178_0041_0000$$$::"Do we have a problem?"[lr]::
23084::$$$message_0178_0041_0001$$$::"Not exactly, I'm just wondering..."[lr]::
23085::$$$message_0178_0041_0002$$$::"Then let's go. Don't forget to stay in your material form."[lr]::
23086::$$$message_0178_0041_0003$$$::There's no stopping her.[lr]::
23087::$$$message_0178_0041_0004$$$::In the end, Bazett bought a meal ticket from the vending machine for two portions of beef bowls and miso soup, and wolfed down the food in barely three minutes before going back outside.[wt canskip=0][current withback=false]::
23088::$$$message_0178_0042_0000$$$::"Hm? Do you have a problem after all?"[lr]::
23089::$$$message_0178_0042_0001$$$::"I just wanna ask... Was the food good?"[lr]::
23090::$$$message_0178_0042_0002$$$::"The portions were large. There was plenty of soup.[lr]::
23091::$$$message_0178_0042_0003$$$::But the fact it took under one minute to serve was wonderful. I should go back there next time."[lr]::
23092::$$$message_0178_0042_0004$$$::That was the entirety of her review.[lr]::
23093::$$$message_0178_0042_0005$$$::To Bazett, meals are nothing but nutritional sustainment.[lr]::
23094::$$$message_0178_0042_0006$$$::How absurdly vulgar.::
23095::$$$message_0178_0043_0000$$$::We investigate the base of an enemy Master we've identified.[lr]::
23096::$$$message_0178_0043_0001$$$::After looking around, we determine that nobody's home.::
23097::$$$message_0178_0044_0000$$$::"Avenger. Can you unlock the door?"[lr]::
23098::$$$message_0178_0044_0001$$$::"Hmm... I can handle simpler locks. But you should have a more reliable way. Aren't you one of the Association's foremost mages?"[lr]::
23099::$$$message_0178_0044_0002$$$::"Lockpicking isn't my specialty. I'll leave it to you."::
23100::$$$message_0178_0045_0000$$$::So sayeth the boss.[lr]::
23101::$$$message_0178_0045_0001$$$::My Master apparently isn't good with delicate tasks. She's made of pure violence.::
23102::$$$message_0178_0046_0000$$$::"Mmkay. This one's tricky, so it'll take some time."[lr]::
23103::$$$message_0178_0046_0001$$$::I stick my arm into a tree trunk planted next to the entrance.[lr]::
23104::$$$message_0178_0046_0002$$$::This is the handy part of being a ghost. I manage to overlay my Magic Circuits onto the magecraft formula.::
23105::$$$message_0178_0047_0000$$$::Ten seconds.[lr]::
23106::$$$message_0178_0047_0001$$$::Twenty seconds.[lr]::
23107::$$$message_0178_0047_0002$$$::Thirty seconds.[lr]::
23108::$$$message_0178_0047_0003$$$::Forty se[line len=2][lr]::
23109::$$$message_0178_0047_0004$$$::"WHOA! W-w-what are you doing!?"[lr]::
23110::$$$message_0178_0047_0005$$$::Goddammit, she just kicked the door in without any warning!::
23111::$$$message_0178_0048_0000$$$::"Infiltrating. Cover me."[lr]::
23112::$$$message_0178_0048_0001$$$::That's all she says in her defense.[lr]::
23113::$$$message_0178_0048_0002$$$::Actually, it's not even an explanation, and this is no "infiltration."[lr]::
23114::$$$message_0178_0048_0003$$$::Bazett adjusts the gloves on her hands and charges into the enemy camp without hesitation.[lr]::
23115::$$$message_0178_0048_0004$$$::Not just absurd and vulgar, but lazy.::
23116::$$$message_0178_0049_0000$$$::"..."[lr]::
23117::$$$message_0178_0049_0001$$$::We finally arrive at the park.[lr]::
23118::$$$message_0178_0049_0002$$$::I'm a little tired physically, but mentally, this really sucks.[lr]::
23119::$$$message_0178_0049_0003$$$::If I turn into spirit form, I can cut out the physical fatigue, but since that isn't possible, I walk in physical form.::
23120::$$$message_0178_0050_0000$$$::"Water, water..."[lr]::
23121::$$$message_0178_0050_0001$$$::I head toward one of the park's water fountains.[lr]::
23122::$$$message_0178_0050_0002$$$::Pale liquid dots the road from here to the top of the hill where we came from.[lr]::
23123::$$$message_0178_0050_0003$$$::As you might've guessed, it's the remnants of the milk that was covering me.::
23124::$$$message_0178_0051_0000$$$::"Hey. Don't get too far away. We're supposed to be working together. Stay near me, Master."[lr]::
23125::$$$message_0178_0051_0001$$$::I turn around.[lr]::
23126::$$$message_0178_0051_0002$$$::"...Pfft."[lr]::
23127::$$$message_0178_0051_0003$$$::Wow, that Bazett is actually laughing.::
23128::$$$message_0178_0052_0000$$$::"Y'know, this is what happens when you get careless. I'm only like this because I shielded my Master from danger.[lr]::
23129::$$$message_0178_0052_0001$$$::Also, I only came this far looking like this because you ordered me not to use the bath in the mansion or any of the houses along the way."[lr]::
23130::$$$message_0178_0052_0002$$$::Look at the reward I get for my loyalty.[lr]::
23131::$$$message_0178_0052_0003$$$::What kinda princess is she?::
23132::$$$message_0178_0053_0000$$$::"I'm grateful. I would look like you now if you hadn't protected me."[lr]::
23133::$$$message_0178_0053_0001$$$::She doesn't sound grateful.[lr]::
23134::$$$message_0178_0053_0002$$$::Damn it, should we hug and make up?::
23135::$$$message_0178_0054_0000$$$::"What's wrong, Avenger? The fountain is that way. Is the milk in your eyes?"[lr]::
23136::$$$message_0178_0054_0001$$$::I wanna [font italic=true]murder[font italic=false] her.[lr]::
23137::$$$message_0178_0054_0002$$$::It might sound like a match between bull and matador, but I'm not letting that walking weapon get her hands on me.::
23138::$$$message_0178_0055_0000$$$::"Tch. Aw shit, I shouldn't have mentioned the trap. This sucks, I missed a funny event.[lr]::
23139::$$$message_0178_0055_0001$$$::...I really regret that. I bet it would've been hilarious to see an un-adorable woman like you get soaked in milk!"[lr]::
23140::$$$message_0178_0055_0002$$$::"Avenger, I order you as your Master to cut the chatter and wash up quickly."[wvs][clfg textoff=0 pos=all rule=シャッター左から time=400]::
23141::$$$message_0178_0056_0000$$$::"Yes, ma'am," I mutter, rinsing the filth off my body.[lr]::
23142::$$$message_0178_0056_0001$$$::Once I get the excess off, I'll be able to turn back into spirit form.[lr]::
23143::$$$message_0178_0056_0002$$$::When the milk hit me, I was forced into physical form and unable to turn back into spirit form.[lr]::
23144::$$$message_0178_0056_0003$$$::Maybe it was an anti-Servant trap, or maybe it would've had a more dramatic effect on a live body.[lr]::
23145::$$$message_0178_0056_0004$$$::Either way, we came up empty-handed in that mansion. It must have been a trap that activates against intruders on the way out.::
23146::$$$message_0178_0057_0000$$$::"...Why cow's milk, though?[lr]::
23147::$$$message_0178_0057_0001$$$::Do people in this country believe that milk repels demons, or something?[lr]::
23148::$$$message_0178_0057_0002$$$::No way. It's gotta be some mean-spirited prank."::
23149::$$$message_0178_0058_0000$$$::"I wonder. But it shows that our opponent is merciful.[lr]::
23150::$$$message_0178_0058_0001$$$::Consider yourself lucky that it happened to be some freshly squeezed milk, Avenger."[lr]::
23151::$$$message_0178_0058_0002$$$::My Master tries to cheer me up, stifling a smile.[lr]::
23152::$$$message_0178_0058_0003$$$::That isn't the problem here.::
23153::$$$message_0178_0059_0000$$$::We continue our patrol.[lr]::
23154::$$$message_0178_0059_0001$$$::Bazett's roaming the town with the dual goals of killing the monsters and looking for Masters.[lr]::
23155::$$$message_0178_0059_0002$$$::What a roundabout way of doing things.[lr]::
23156::$$$message_0178_0059_0003$$$::This isn't what you'd do if you want to win the Holy Grail War.[lr]::
23157::$$$message_0178_0059_0004$$$::Bazett is searching for neither of those things,[lr]::
23158::$$$message_0178_0059_0005$$$::and she doesn't even realize it herself.::
23159::$$$message_0178_0060_0000$$$::She's probably worried because she can't forget it. She should take a page from a certain idiot who's forgotten his own abilities.::
23160::$$$message_0178_0061_0000$$$::"..."[lr]::
23161::$$$message_0178_0061_0001$$$::Something's off.[lr]::
23162::$$$message_0178_0061_0002$$$::Bazett goes quiet staring at the sea, as if the harbor dredges up bad memories.::
23163::$$$message_0178_0062_0000$$$::"Avenger, we've fought many Masters.[lr]::
23164::$$$message_0178_0062_0001$$$::Not to mention the encounters with Saber, Archer, Caster, Rider, Assassin, and yourself.[lr]::
23165::$$$message_0178_0062_0002$$$::The only enemies we haven't met directly are the Einzbern Master and Servant."[lr]::
23166::$$$message_0178_0062_0003$$$::"Yeah, just about. Though it sounds less impressive when you consider our win-loss record."::
23167::$$$message_0178_0063_0000$$$::"...Yes. We haven't achieved a single clear victory yet. That's nothing to boast about, even if we're fighting overpowered familiars."[lr]::
23168::$$$message_0178_0063_0001$$$::I hear her grinding her teeth.[lr]::
23169::$$$message_0178_0063_0002$$$::Yet it isn't out of frustration. More like urging herself forward.::
23170::$$$message_0178_0064_0000$$$::"I know the outlook isn't good, but I still want to hear your opinion.[lr]::
23171::$$$message_0178_0064_0001$$$::...Do you think we can win?[lr]::
23172::$$$message_0178_0064_0002$$$::It's true we lack raw power, but if we keep repeating this, eventually..."::
23173::$$$message_0178_0065_0000$$$::[font italic=true]We might be the last pair left standing[font italic=false] is what her gaze tells me.[lr]::
23174::$$$message_0178_0065_0001$$$::We're losing because we still lack experience.[lr]::
23175::$$$message_0178_0065_0002$$$::Bazett's been using me to fight to some extent, and if I tell her my true Noble Phantasm, there's no Servant we can't beat.::
23176::$$$message_0178_0066_0000$$$::...Though, there's no need to tell her now. She'll figure out how we can win soon enough, whether she wants to or not.[lr]::
23177::$$$message_0178_0066_0001$$$::"I think that eventually, we'll stop losing.[lr]::
23178::$$$message_0178_0066_0002$$$::But before that, I noticed you started saying 'we' instead of 'I,' Master."[lr]::
23179::$$$message_0178_0066_0003$$$::I mention it because I think it's funny.::
23180::$$$message_0178_0067_0000$$$::"Ah... O-oh, really? I wasn't really conscious of it."[lr]::
23181::$$$message_0178_0067_0001$$$::"That's even funnier. It means you've unconsciously begun to trust me.[lr]::
23182::$$$message_0178_0067_0002$$$::You in love? Should I take it as one of those 'friends-to-lovers' developments?"::
23183::$$$message_0178_0068_0000$$$::"S-stop joking around and finish answering the question.[lr]::
23184::$$$message_0178_0068_0001$$$::What proof do you have that we won't lose anymore? Give me your honest answer, and don't hide anything."::
23185::$$$message_0178_0069_0000$$$::"I ain't got proof, but we'll start to see results in time.[lr]::
23186::$$$message_0178_0069_0001$$$::You have a trump card that can beat Servants, right?[lr]::
23187::$$$message_0178_0069_0002$$$::In the same sense, I have one that can slow them down a little.[lr]::
23188::$$$message_0178_0069_0003$$$::It just depends on how we use them both. We just need to work together."::
23189::$$$message_0178_0070_0000$$$::"A trump card...?[lr]::
23190::$$$message_0178_0070_0001$$$::Do you have multiple Noble Phantasms?"[lr]::
23191::$$$message_0178_0070_0002$$$::"Nope, just the one. The resurrection isn't me, but something tacked on as part of Aŋra Mainiiu.[lr]::
23192::$$$message_0178_0070_0003$$$::My Noble Phantasm is a fake version of Avesta, Universally Transcribed Creation. I'll tell you about it once we get home."::
23193::$$$message_0178_0071_0000$$$::Avesta is a support-type Noble Phantasm that can independently record events which have occurred. It's like an autonomous typewriter, so it's completely worthless in a fight.[lr]::
23194::$$$message_0178_0071_0001$$$::Avesta's advantage is that it can transcribe inarticulate emotions and emotions people aren't even aware of into writing.[lr]::
23195::$$$message_0178_0071_0002$$$::It's a document that accurately records everything[line len=2]a Noble Phantasm that doesn't hurt anyone, worthy of its namesake, the holy scripture.[lr]::
23196::$$$message_0178_0071_0003$$$::And my Noble Phantasm is an unremarkable counterfeit.::
23197::$$$message_0178_0072_0000$$$::"Anyway, you need to get serious if you don't want to keep losing.[lr]::
23198::$$$message_0178_0072_0001$$$::You're the strongest fighter of all the Masters.[lr]::
23199::$$$message_0178_0072_0002$$$::You could beat a Servant barehanded if it came down to it, so why don't you have more faith in yourself?"::
23200::$$$message_0178_0073_0000$$$::"Well, I... It's true that I don't consider myself inferior to a Servant, but all I can do is fight.[lr]::
23201::$$$message_0178_0073_0001$$$::In all other respects, I think I'm the least skilled of all the Masters."::
23202::$$$message_0178_0074_0000$$$::"And what's wrong with that?[lr]::
23203::$$$message_0178_0074_0001$$$::Why do you feel guilty about being [font italic=true]shredded?[font italic=false] That's pathetic in itself."[lr]::
23204::$$$message_0178_0074_0002$$$::"Wha... I-I don't feel guilty.[lr]::
23205::$$$message_0178_0074_0003$$$::I don't regret any of the lives I've taken."::
23206::$$$message_0178_0075_0000$$$::"What a reliable iron maiden. Try and keep that spirit up.[lr]::
23207::$$$message_0178_0075_0001$$$::In fact, if you try any harder, I'll start to lose face. Even now, you're still ten times stronger than I am."::
23208::$$$message_0178_0076_0000$$$::"Y-yes, I'm aware of that.[lr]::
23209::$$$message_0178_0076_0001$$$::I learned a painful lesson on the first day not to expect much from you in combat."[lr]::
23210::$$$message_0178_0076_0002$$$::"Yup, yup. Oh, but I'm still number one when it comes to killing people. Everyone's got stuff they're good and bad at.[lr]::
23211::$$$message_0178_0076_0003$$$::...Oh, I guess not number one. Worldwide, I'm in second or third place."::
23212::$$$message_0178_0077_0000$$$::"Huh? There are others better than you at killing people?"[lr]::
23213::$$$message_0178_0077_0001$$$::"Sure are. The dog and the spider. I can't keep up with those two, no matter what I do. Quality aside, they're just on a different level in terms of sheer speed."::
23214::$$$message_0178_0078_0000$$$::I've never met or competed with them, but I know the hard facts.[lr]::
23215::$$$message_0178_0078_0001$$$::I know them like a spider spinning its nest as soon as it's born.[lr]::
23216::$$$message_0178_0078_0002$$$::I learned that unshakable truth as soon as they started calling me Aŋra Mainiiu.::
23217::$$$message_0178_0079_0000$$$::"Hm. So as a Heroic Spirit, you're somehow limited in your speed.[lr]::
23218::$$$message_0178_0079_0001$$$::Avenger. You mentioned that Aŋra Mainiiu was a name assigned to you, so it must not be your True Name. What was your name when you were alive?"::
23219::$$$message_0178_0080_0000$$$::"I said I don't know.[lr]::
23220::$$$message_0178_0080_0001$$$::I don't have a name. If Aŋra Mainiiu is hard to say, you can just call me Aŋra."::
23221::$$$message_0178_0081_0000$$$::"That can't be true. You should at least be able to remember your own name.[lr]::
23222::$$$message_0178_0081_0001$$$::...No, I suppose I'm not one to talk, but everything begins with a name.[lr]::
23223::$$$message_0178_0081_0002$$$::The name you were given at your birth represents the rest of your life. If you can't remember it, you wouldn't be able to whistle in such a carefree manner."::
23224::$$$message_0178_0082_0000$$$::"You just don't get it. My name is [font italic=true]gone[font italic=false]. It was stripped from me once they started treating me as a hero.[lr]::
23225::$$$message_0178_0082_0001$$$::Curses were the one thing my village excelled at. They magically took my name from me, so I don't know the name I was born with, nor what people called me before then.[lr]::
23226::$$$message_0178_0082_0002$$$::You can tell me to remember, but that information doesn't exist anywhere in the world anymore."::
23227::$$$message_0178_0083_0000$$$::A name represents the rest of your life, huh?[lr]::
23228::$$$message_0178_0083_0001$$$::That's very poetic, Bazett. I can't let you get the last word in, so I'll tell a story.::
23229::$$$message_0178_0084_0000$$$::It's an old tale that happens often.[lr]::
23230::$$$message_0178_0084_0001$$$::A man had his life saved by a friend. The friend died saving the man.[lr]::
23231::$$$message_0178_0084_0002$$$::The man started using his dead friend's name, and went on to save many more people.[lr]::
23232::$$$message_0178_0084_0003$$$::He hoped that the credit for his life and achievements would go to his dead friend.::
23233::$$$message_0178_0085_0000$$$::There's nothing pretty about that at all.[lr]::
23234::$$$message_0178_0085_0001$$$::In other words, the man died as soon as he began falsely using his friend's name.::
23235::$$$message_0178_0086_0000$$$::"Then, your original name is..."[lr]::
23236::$$$message_0178_0086_0001$$$::"Gone. But I like what people call me now. They've been using it a lot longer than my birth name.[lr]::
23237::$$$message_0178_0086_0002$$$::Guess you could say I'm fond of it. I think it's pretty fitting."::
23238::$$$message_0178_0087_0000$$$::"I see. You lost your birth name, but you've grown attached to the name people called you as a hero.[lr]::
23239::$$$message_0178_0087_0001$$$::It may only be a title, but it was an accolade given by the people. It makes sense you'd like it.[lr]::
23240::$$$message_0178_0087_0002$$$::...I'm sorry. You deserve an apology. I was condescending and jumped to conclusions."::
23241::$$$message_0178_0088_0000$$$::"Hmm... [wvl canskip=false time=800]Well, you don't need to worry about it, and it's not worth an apology."[lr]::
23242::$$$message_0178_0088_0001$$$::Jumping to conclusions is good, but pity isn't. If you're going to express sympathy, then do it with more love. Please love me, baby.::
23243::$$$message_0178_0089_0000$$$::"You can make it up to me by answering my question.[lr]::
23244::$$$message_0178_0089_0001$$$::You said that a name is a life. Your full name is so overblown. Sounds like there must be some posh story behind it."[lr]::
23245::$$$message_0178_0089_0002$$$::"Y-you want to know about my past?[lr]::
23246::$$$message_0178_0089_0003$$$::We'd better not get into that. I'm sure it'll bore you. You won't find it[line len=2]"::
23247::$$$message_0178_0090_0000$$$::"Boring stories are fine.[lr]::
23248::$$$message_0178_0090_0001$$$::C'mon, you're sorry, aren't you? It's okay. Anything's interesting to me, as long as I haven't heard it before."[lr]::
23249::$$$message_0178_0090_0002$$$::"...All right. Loose lips really do sink ships, as they say."::
23250::$$$message_0178_0091_0000$$$::You've got that right.[lr]::
23251::$$$message_0178_0091_0001$$$::A lot of those sunken ships end up having pretty delicious endings, though.[lr]::
23252::$$$message_0178_0091_0002$$$::I hope my Master's got some hidden treats in store.::
23253::$$$message_0178_0092_0000$$$::"That's all for my personal history. Are you satisfied?"[lr]::
23254::$$$message_0178_0092_0001$$$::"...Well, I got all that, objectively."::
23255::$$$message_0178_0093_0000$$$::   Bazett's account of her background stuck to the facts.[lr]::
23256::$$$message_0178_0093_0001$$$::Apparently, her family is an old lineage of mages dating back to the Age of Gods.[lr]::
23257::$$$message_0178_0093_0002$$$::They were originally notable Runecasters who served the gods, and were entrusted with some unique secrets that the other families weren't privy to.[wt canskip=0]::
23258::$$$message_0178_0094_0000$$$::In other words, they were the elite of the elite.[lr]::
23259::$$$message_0178_0094_0001$$$::But, they were based in an utter backwater, and they weren't big enough to resemble a clan.[lr]::
23260::$$$message_0178_0094_0002$$$::They were elite, but not prosperous or well-known.[lr]::
23261::$$$message_0178_0094_0003$$$::They may have possessed the highest form of authority in the magical world, but in real life, it meant that they ran a rural school where only one child per generation could inherit the family secrets.::
23262::$$$message_0178_0095_0000$$$::Bazett was the heir of her generation, and worked her entire life to learn the family secrets. Eventually, she learned to reproduce them as a matter of course, just like her ancestors.[lr]::
23263::$$$message_0178_0095_0001$$$::She was a Gods' Holder[line len=2]a carrier of transmissible lore.[wt canskip=0][lr]::
23264::$$$message_0178_0095_0002$$$::She possessed a magecraft attribute passed down since the Age of Gods, something other than Magic Circuits. It's a wonder they managed to preserve it over the millennia.[lr]::
23265::$$$message_0178_0095_0003$$$::Though from the way she described it, it sounds more like a pathogen kept alive over generations, rather than a hereditary trait.[wdash canskip=0]::
23266::$$$message_0178_0096_0000$$$::Once Bazett came of age, she was granted the name Fraga. She doesn't explain her reasons for joining the Mage's Association.[lr]::
23267::$$$message_0178_0096_0001$$$::I can still infer why.[lr]::
23268::$$$message_0178_0096_0002$$$::Knowing how hard she is on herself, she must have wanted more opportunities to train herself.[lr]::
23269::$$$message_0178_0096_0003$$$::Against her parents' wishes, she contacted the Association, which invited this unexpected yet notable lineage into its ranks.[lr]::
23270::$$$message_0178_0096_0004$$$::The Association welcomed a new comrade who could transmit lost secrets, and Bazett was greeted with much fanfare.[wt canskip=0]::
23271::$$$message_0178_0097_0000$$$::However...[lr]::
23272::$$$message_0178_0097_0001$$$::Apparently, the warm welcome was only on paper, and she didn't have a place in the Association.::
23273::$$$message_0178_0098_0000$$$::For all their elitism, mages are a fiercely competitive bunch. The Mage's Association might have preserved its power for centuries, but internally, it's plagued with political intrigue and power struggles.[lr]::
23274::$$$message_0178_0098_0001$$$::They want more prestige on the world stage, but someone on the inside who shines too brightly is even less desirable than a talentless minion.[lr]::
23275::$$$message_0178_0098_0002$$$::To get to the crux of it...[lr]::
23276::$$$message_0178_0098_0003$$$::It's been centuries since the Association has had any room for a new noble family.::
23277::$$$message_0178_0099_0000$$$::Still, Bazett tried her best.[lr]::
23278::$$$message_0178_0099_0001$$$::She tried so hard at the Association which didn't really want her, but her achievements made her an outcast, and they began to treat her as a particularly conspicuous tumor. Eventually, she was sent to the front lines to get her out of their hair.[lr]::
23279::$$$message_0178_0099_0002$$$::She became a Seal Designation Enforcer.[lr]::
23280::$$$message_0178_0099_0003$$$::Being an Enforcer is a job for the Mage's Association's vaunted mages who have well and truly lost their marbles, akin to the heretic-hunting Executors of the Holy Church.::
23281::$$$message_0178_0100_0000$$$::For those mages with particularly rare talents, or who have broken a taboo, a Seal Designation means that they are to be restrained and remain in captivity for life under the guise of "preserving" their knowledge.[lr]::
23282::$$$message_0178_0100_0001$$$::Bazett was chosen to enforce such orders.[lr]::
23283::$$$message_0178_0100_0002$$$::For years, she's been single-mindedly traveling the world handling cases for the Association, dutifully executing every mission even though the pay isn't worth it.::
23284::$$$message_0178_0101_0000$$$::That's the life story of Bazett Fraga McRemitz.[lr]::
23285::$$$message_0178_0101_0001$$$::There's a lot to unpack, but if I had to remark on one thing...::
23286::$$$message_0178_0102_0000$$$::"And yet still no love life. You spent all your time chasing magecraft?[lr]::
23287::$$$message_0178_0102_0001$$$::Didn't you at least get one boy toy back home?"[lr]::
23288::$$$message_0178_0102_0002$$$::"No. There wasn't any need for one."[lr]::
23289::$$$message_0178_0102_0003$$$::"Need? C'mon. Everyone's got someone, even if they don't [font italic=true]need[font italic=false] them. Wasn't it boring?"::
23290::$$$message_0178_0103_0000$$$::"I'm used to solitude.[lr]::
23291::$$$message_0178_0103_0001$$$::It isn't as lonesome as you think, and even if I don't feel quite complete, I'm doing just fine right now."[lr]::
23292::$$$message_0178_0103_0002$$$::"Ahhh..."[lr]::
23293::$$$message_0178_0103_0003$$$::She's a severe patient, this one.[lr]::
23294::$$$message_0178_0103_0004$$$::Need? Lonesome? Feeling complete? What a pain this woman is.[lr]::
23295::$$$message_0178_0103_0005$$$::She's just never had a man in her life.::
23296::$$$message_0178_0104_0000$$$::"Hmm. You a virgin?"[lr]::
23297::$$$message_0178_0104_0001$$$::I stare my partner down.[lr]::
23298::$$$message_0178_0104_0002$$$::Like a squirrel nibbling on a walnut. Earnestly. Diligently. And at times, scathingly.::
23299::$$$message_0178_0105_0000$$$::"Urgh..."[lr]::
23300::$$$message_0178_0105_0001$$$::My Master takes a half step back.::
23301::$$$message_0178_0106_0000$$$::"I-I have experience through work, so I don't understand your question. What does that have to do with the Holy Grail War?"[lr]::
23302::$$$message_0178_0106_0001$$$::Oh, she does.[lr]::
23303::$$$message_0178_0106_0002$$$::That's all well and good, but I wasn't asking her to make fun of her.[lr]::
23304::$$$message_0178_0106_0003$$$::But her response made me laugh because it actually is slightly relevant to the war.::
23305::$$$message_0178_0107_0000$$$::"It does have something to do with the war. It's a question of how strong you are as a human being.[lr]::
23306::$$$message_0178_0107_0001$$$::Listen, Master. Don't underestimate passion. It's the strongest motivator there is."[lr]::
23307::$$$message_0178_0107_0002$$$::Okay, vengeance ranks up there too, but it doesn't leave anything once it's finished.[lr]::
23308::$$$message_0178_0107_0003$$$::It's explosively powerful, yet unproductive, so all in all it gets a Fail.::
23309::$$$message_0178_0108_0000$$$::"I-I don't know what you're getting at. All I can see is that you're having a laugh at my expense.[lr]::
23310::$$$message_0178_0108_0001$$$::Enough of this mischief, Aŋra Mai[line len=2]"::
23311::$$$message_0178_0109_0000$$$::"This is totally serious.[lr]::
23312::$$$message_0178_0109_0001$$$::I'm talking about love, here. It's basically the ultimate force. Haven't you ever heard that people can only grow strong thanks to love?[lr]::
23313::$$$message_0178_0109_0002$$$::From the looks of it, you lack that basic concept.[lr]::
23314::$$$message_0178_0109_0003$$$::As someone fighting by you, it's been bothering me."[lr]::
23315::$$$message_0178_0109_0004$$$::I answer her seriously.[lr]::
23316::$$$message_0178_0109_0005$$$::"..."[lr]::
23317::$$$message_0178_0109_0006$$$::She's listening earnestly.::
23318::$$$message_0178_0110_0000$$$::"I-I don't believe you. Your idea of love is wicked.[lr]::
23319::$$$message_0178_0110_0001$$$::B-besides, it isn't something to be discussed lightly."[lr]::
23320::$$$message_0178_0110_0002$$$::She seems to think it would cheapen the emotion.[lr]::
23321::$$$message_0178_0110_0003$$$::That's cute.::
23322::$$$message_0178_0111_0000$$$::"And why is that? We can talk about it. It's nothing to be ashamed of.[lr]::
23323::$$$message_0178_0111_0001$$$::Saying you want to be loved isn't an expression of loneliness. It says that you enjoy it, so you want more.[lr]::
23324::$$$message_0178_0111_0002$$$::'I love you' is a perfectly normal expression, right?[lr]::
23325::$$$message_0178_0111_0003$$$::Or what, you dislike everyone you meet? That's like going out of your way to make enemies."::
23326::$$$message_0178_0112_0000$$$::"Very well. I'll take it as advice.[lr]::
23327::$$$message_0178_0112_0001$$$::...Honestly, you have a way with words, even though you're a child."[lr]::
23328::$$$message_0178_0112_0002$$$::"Thanks. But I'm a brat, not a child. Not an adult either, though."[lr]::
23329::$$$message_0178_0112_0003$$$::All I'm trying to say is that I'm no longer a child.::
23330::$$$message_0178_0113_0000$$$::"Perhaps. To me, you just seem like an impudent boy. Around five years younger than me."[lr]::
23331::$$$message_0178_0113_0001$$$::"Really? How old are you, Master?"[lr]::
23332::$$$message_0178_0113_0002$$$::"Twenty-three. What about it?"[lr]::
23333::$$$message_0178_0113_0003$$$::"No way! You're that young!?[lr]::
23334::$$$message_0178_0113_0004$$$::I'd pegged you at around thirty!"[lr]::
23335::$$$message_0178_0113_0005$$$::Oh. Her murder meter just shot up.::
23336::$$$message_0178_0114_0000$$$::"...How amusing. What do you base that on, Avenger?"[lr]::
23337::$$$message_0178_0114_0001$$$::Loose lips sink ships, indeed.::
23338::$$$message_0178_0115_0000$$$::"...Well, you've got a lot of life experience. You're too damn good at your job. When'd you start working?"[lr]::
23339::$$$message_0178_0115_0001$$$::"...Around age fifteen. It wasn't too early. I was already well-trained by that point, so my abilities weren't in question."::
23340::$$$message_0178_0116_0000$$$::"Haah. And I bet you've been wearing the same clothes since.[lr]::
23341::$$$message_0178_0116_0001$$$::I guess you would be pretty set in your ways, after twenty-three years."[lr]::
23342::$$$message_0178_0116_0002$$$::I believe her now. She's wearing a well-worn, if exquisite, suit of armor.::
23343::$$$message_0178_0117_0000$$$::"What are you talking about? I just said that my career is eight years long."[lr]::
23344::$$$message_0178_0117_0001$$$::"I'm talking about how long you've worn that suit of armor. How long you've been this socially awkward.[lr]::
23345::$$$message_0178_0117_0002$$$::...You know, if the average length of childhood is ten years, that would already make you thirty-three."::
23346::$$$message_0178_0118_0000$$$::"You were already a ten-year-old grown-up at birth, so that puts you just over the big three-zero.[lr]::
23347::$$$message_0178_0118_0001$$$::Saying that you're twice my current age is... Wait, whaddya know? My guess was right on the mark after all."[lr]::
23348::$$$message_0178_0118_0002$$$::I give her a stately nod.[lr]::
23349::$$$message_0178_0118_0003$$$::Bazett just stands there, speechless. Maybe she's fed up with me.::
23350::$$$message_0178_0119_0000$$$::"Break time is over. We're heading back out into town."[lr]::
23351::$$$message_0178_0119_0001$$$::"Aye-aye. I guess we'll just keep dwelling on the past, like we always do."[lr]::
23352::$$$message_0178_0119_0002$$$::Bazett walks out in front of me.::
23353::$$$message_0178_0120_0000$$$::"...You're making a fool out of me."[lr]::
23354::$$$message_0178_0120_0001$$$::"Yeah? Because you [font italic=true]are[font italic=false] a fool."[lr]::
23355::$$$message_0178_0120_0002$$$::I think we make a balanced team.[lr]::
23356::$$$message_0178_0120_0003$$$::On the one hand, a brat who isn't a child anymore.[lr]::
23357::$$$message_0178_0120_0004$$$::On the other, a fool who threw away her childhood.::
23358::$$$message_0178_0121_0000$$$::"Huh? Hey, Master!"[lr]::
23359::$$$message_0178_0121_0001$$$::Bazett's stopped walking.[lr]::
23360::$$$message_0178_0121_0002$$$::She's standing stock-still, like she found something.::
23361::$$$message_0178_0122_0000$$$::"What is it? [cacheimage storage=バゼット05a(中)][wvl][movefg textoff=0 opacity=255 time=700 pos=c accel=-2 storage=バゼット05a(中)]Did you spot something, Master?"[lr]::
23362::$$$message_0178_0122_0001$$$::I walk up to her curiously.[lr]::
23363::$$$message_0178_0122_0002$$$::    And then...[wm canskip=0][wm canskip=0][clfg textoff=0 time=10 storage=バゼット05a(遠)][lr]::
23364::$$$message_0178_0122_0003$$$::"...I know something's wrong with me.[lr]::
23365::$$$message_0178_0122_0004$$$::I hate to admit it, but you're right, Aŋra Mainiiu.[lr]::
23366::$$$message_0178_0122_0005$$$::I am a fool. I can't deny it, when you put it that bluntly."[lr]::
23367::$$$message_0178_0122_0006$$$::She says it in a normal tone.::
23368::$$$message_0178_0123_0000$$$::"...[wait canskip=false time=800][say storage=snplg03_anr_0560 name=アンリ]No one's ever told you that before, then."[lr]::
23369::$$$message_0178_0123_0001$$$::"Yes. I've never had anyone around me who talks to me as directly as you do."[lr]::
23370::$$$message_0178_0123_0002$$$::This chick has rotten luck.[lr]::
23371::$$$message_0178_0123_0003$$$::There's no shortage of beta dudes who could tell her that, but she's never gotten involved with a single one.::
23372::$$$message_0178_0124_0000$$$::"I had no idea. When someone points out your weakness, it also means that he sees you for who you are. A little irritating, I'll admit, but it does make me feel better.[lr]::
23373::$$$message_0178_0124_0001$$$::...Yeah. I can actually relax with you. It isn't fair that I'm the only tense one all the time."::
23374::$$$message_0178_0125_0000$$$::"..."[lr]::
23375::$$$message_0178_0125_0001$$$::I can't help but stare.[lr]::
23376::$$$message_0178_0125_0002$$$::Among all the sights I could get bored of, this one is a rare one, and it can only happen here.::
23377::$$$message_0178_0126_0000$$$::"Let's go, Aŋra Mainiiu. We're checking the industrial area of Shinto next."[lr]::
23378::$$$message_0178_0126_0001$$$::"Roger that, Master. And you can just call me Aŋra. It's a mouthful, isn't it?"::
23379::$$$message_0178_0127_0000$$$::"Hm? It makes no difference to me.[lr]::
23380::$$$message_0178_0127_0001$$$::...If you'd prefer I shorten it, I can call you Aŋra. But it sounds a tad plain, if you ask me.[lr]::
23381::$$$message_0178_0127_0002$$$::It just sounds commonplace. Unworthy of a Heroic Spirit."::
23382::$$$message_0178_0128_0000$$$::"You get hung up on the weirdest things.[lr]::
23383::$$$message_0178_0128_0001$$$::...A-ha. So it bothers you because your name isn't normal, either.[lr]::
23384::$$$message_0178_0128_0002$$$::I'd just as soon have the contrast[line len=2]oh, but we both have men's names."[lr]::
23385::$$$message_0178_0128_0003$$$::My name's definitely boring, but it's adorable compared to my Master's.[lr]::
23386::$$$message_0178_0128_0004$$$::There's nothing pretty about "Bazett." It's harsh and devoid of any feminine charm.::
23387::$$$message_0178_0129_0000$$$::"...Aŋra Mainiiu, I believe I said that a person's name is their life.[lr]::
23388::$$$message_0178_0129_0001$$$::I hope you're ready for the consequences of laughing at mine."[lr]::
23389::$$$message_0178_0129_0002$$$::"Not at all. I'm not ready, nor do I have a problem with your name."[lr]::
23390::$$$message_0178_0129_0003$$$::"Very good. This topic is now off-limits."::
23391::$$$message_0178_0130_0000$$$::With that, we return to the Holy Grail War.[lr]::
23392::$$$message_0178_0130_0001$$$::The night patrol is enjoyable, as far as such things can be.[lr]::
23393::$$$message_0178_0130_0002$$$::I've started to understand how it feels for days to sluggishly pass by.[lr]::
23394::$$$message_0178_0130_0003$$$::But I only understand it. I don't [font italic=true]own[font italic=false] it.::
23395::$$$message_0178_0131_0000$$$::The nights will continue as long as someone wishes for them.[lr]::
23396::$$$message_0178_0131_0001$$$::I and the woman I'm contracted with are unconsciously prolonging this war.[lr]::
23397::$$$message_0178_0131_0002$$$::It's on repeat, with no end or sequel.::
23398::$$$message_0178_0132_0000$$$::Regardless, its radiance will eventually fade.[lr]::
23399::$$$message_0178_0132_0001$$$::Once only its shape is left, its color will grow muddy.[lr]::
23400::$$$message_0178_0132_0002$$$::Something you've seen before won't have the same fresh glow to it after you've seen it once.[lr]::
23401::$$$message_0178_0132_0003$$$::Just like a solar eclipse.[lr]::
23402::$$$message_0178_0132_0004$$$::It turns black and never shines again.::
23403::$$$message_0178_0133_0000$$$::"...Hah."[lr]::
23404::$$$message_0178_0133_0001$$$::I feel a little silly.[lr]::
23405::$$$message_0178_0133_0002$$$::Thinking about whose wish it is exactly won't change a thing.:P@t